      "why": "the contract's only multi-parameter method. Every other one takes 0 or 1 argument, so argument POSITION had no coverage — nor did a bstr sitting anywhere but first. The digest `i=<dec>|s=<utf8>|b=<hex>` pins each value AND its slot in one comparison: swap two arguments and it changes. A container return would confound slot correctness with container encoding.",
